conduct of, during the siege of the Pyrucheium, 318; writings of, 319, 320;
Paschal canons of, 319; Institutes of, 320; death of, 320.

Baptism, 151 (note 16); clinical, received by Novatus, 288;
called “seal” (σφραγίς), 289;
discussion regarding baptism of heretics, 294–297; of the Church, rejected by
Novatus, 297.

Gospels, Irenæus on the, 222; of Matthew, see Matthew;
of Mark, see Mark; of Luke, see Luke; of John, see John;
order of, 152, 155; of the Nazarenes, see Nazarenes; according to the
Hebrews, see Hebrews, Gospel of; of Peter, see Peter; order of
the, according to Clement, 261; the four, 273; used by the Elkesites, 280.

Hegesippus, memoirs of, used by Eusebius, 81 (note 5);
account of death of James, the Lord’s brother, 125–127; visits Rome, 184, 198;
